! GAPS corpus-coverage deck (family=modes): HARMONICMODET / sequential-time
! harmonics (Pascal TSolutionAlgs.SolveHarmonicT, SolutionAlgs.pas:1097 —
! "Sequential-Time Harmonics"). UNCOVERED by any other modes deck. It combines a
! time step (IntervalHrs) with the frequency sweep: each of the number=3 steps
! re-runs InitializeForHarmonics (loads/sources re-seeded at that step's
! loadshape multiplier), RetrieveSavedVoltages restores the fundamental, then the
! DoAllHarmonics fan-out sweeps the collected spectrum. The load's daily shape
! modulates the per-step harmonic injection.
! Boundary pinned: the HarmonicT dispatch (harmonics.rs solve_harmonic_t) + the
! per-step re-seed; compared via the per-step/per-harmonic monitor samples.
! Feature-sensitive vs plain HARMONICMODE (identical spectra, single sweep) via
! the harmonicT dispatch itself. NOTE: the daily shape does NOT change the
! compared output on the oracle (flattened-shape fingerprint is bit-identical) —
! the injection derives from the saved fundamental; shape-sensitivity is not
! part of this deck's proof basis.
Clear
New Circuit.gaps_harmt basekv=12.47 phases=3 bus1=sourcebus mvasc3=200 mvasc1=210
New Loadshape.d3 npts=3 interval=1 mult=(0.70 1.00 0.85)
New Spectrum.sp5 numharm=4 harmonic=(1 5 7 11) %mag=(100 16 11 7) angle=(0 0 0 0)
New Line.l1 bus1=sourcebus bus2=b1 phases=3 r1=0.30 x1=0.90 r0=0.9 x0=2.7 c1=3.0 c0=1.5 length=2 units=km
New Line.l2 bus1=b1 bus2=b2 phases=3 r1=0.35 x1=0.95 r0=1.0 x0=2.8 c1=3.0 c0=1.5 length=1.5 units=km
New Load.ld1 bus1=b1 phases=3 kv=12.47 kw=700 pf=0.95 model=1 spectrum=sp5 daily=d3
New Monitor.m_h element=Line.l2 terminal=1 mode=0
Set voltagebases=[12.47]
Calcvoltagebases
Solve
! Sequential-time harmonics: 3 time steps, each sweeping the collected spectrum.
Set mode=harmonicT stepsize=1h number=3
Solve
